    crm:P183i_has_representation <https://ids.lib.harvard.edu/ids/iiif/493313465/full/full/0/default.jpg> ;
    rdf:value """Tuesday, June 4, 1907
Cool. Fine.
Ray’s 20th Birthday!!
Bernhard and I grappled with the Gargiolli photographs and their awfully unsystematic catalogue.
Hutchins Hapgood came to lunch, great dear that he always is.
Poor Karin got quite deaf , but kept cheerful. She and I called on Mrs. Harter, and the Count of Turin came in, and was very jolly.
We all dined at Gamberaia, for Miss Blood’s birthday. We dined on the terrace. It was beautiful, but rather cool."""^^xsd:string ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:index 177 ;
    mbdiaries-ontology:part_of <https://mbdiaries.itatti.harvard.edu/resource/diary/1907> .

